{"ts": "2026-11-02T16:17:47.534921Z", "run_id": "r-20261102T1616Z-9af8", "unit": "openspec:add-web-flow-graph", "seq": 8, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-003", "id": "Q-003", "status": "answered", "reason": "The criterion is a unit-level check of layoutFlow return values and two constants; nothing in it is observable through the page, so the step 5 not_testable verdict is correct and the hold can be waived. The committed Node test asserts each item of the scenario against the layouts written out in the test, and I compared those layouts with reference.md § Layouts for S, SLASH and ONE (coordinates, labels, paths, width, height, layers) and read layout.ts to confirm the implementation yields them and does not mutate the document.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "H-d0c803fb", "kind": "verdict", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.28095575, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "f875058264c99b929dc797f71014f56eef9af187b6d43358b23fe2ed8d467ec8", "checked": [{"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.test.ts:256", "quote": "test(\"C-c1de3761 layers order coordinates and labels of a small flow\", () => {", "claim": "A Node test traces criterion C-c1de3761."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.test.ts:257", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(resultOf(flowS(), \"S\"), { status: \"ok\", layout: S_LAYOUT });", "claim": "The test deep-compares the first S result with the ok result and the S layout."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.test.ts:258", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(layoutOf(withReversedNodeKeys(flowS()), \"S reversed\"), S_LAYOUT);", "claim": "The reversed-key run is checked to equal the first layout."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.test.ts:259", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(layoutOf(deepFreeze(flowS()), \"S frozen\"), S_LAYOUT);", "claim": "The deep-frozen run is checked not to throw and to equal the first layout."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.test.ts:262", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(GRAPH_GEOMETRY, { nodeWidth: 160, nodeHeight: 48, gapX: 32, gapY: 56, margin: 16 });", "claim": "The geometry constant is asserted with the figures of the scenario."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.test.ts:263", "quote": "assert.equal(MAX_GRAPH_NODES, 200);", "claim": "The node bound is asserted to be 200."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.test.ts:216", "quote": "label: \"a/b, c~d, default\",", "claim": "The SLASH expectation carries the merged label of several paths."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.test.ts:177", "quote": "width: 384,\n  height: 392,\n  layers: 4,", "claim": "The S layout expected by the test has the width, height and layer count of reference.md."}, {"ref": "spec:reference.md", "quote": "**S**: width 384, height 392, layers 4, start \"a\". Nodes: a 0 0 112 16 [b]; b 1 0 112 120 [c, d]; c 2 0 16 224 [e]; d 2 1 208 224 []; e 3 0 112 328 [].", "claim": "The reference figures for S match the nodes and dimensions written in the test."}, {"ref": "spec:reference.md", "quote": "**SLASH**: width 192, height 184. One edge a b with label \"a/b, c~d, default\", paths `/cases/a~1b`, `/cases/c~0d`, `/default`, coordinates 96 64 96 120 96 92.", "claim": "The reference SLASH section matches the SLASH layout in the test."}, {"ref": "spec:reference.md", "quote": "**ONE**: width 192, height 80, layers 1, a at 16 16.", "claim": "The reference ONE section matches the ONE layout in the test."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.ts:9", "quote": "} = { nodeWidth: 160, nodeHeight: 48, gapX: 32, gapY: 56, margin: 16 };", "claim": "The implementation defines the geometry constant with the required values."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.ts:11", "quote": "export const MAX_GRAPH_NODES: number = 200;", "claim": "The implementation sets the bound to 200."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.ts:168", "quote": "const ids = entries.map(([id]) => id).sort(compareIds);", "claim": "Ids are sorted by code unit, so key order does not change the layout."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.ts:179", "quote": "const nodeMap = new Map<string, unknown>(entries);", "claim": "Nodes are read through a Map built from the entries and the document is never written, so a frozen copy does not throw."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.ts:153", "quote": "if (labels.length === 1 && labels[0] === \"next\") return null;", "claim": "A lone next successor gives a null label as the ONE and S sections require."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.ts:142", "quote": "return path.slice(\"/cases/\".length).replace(/~1/g, \"/\").replace(/~0/g, \"~\");", "claim": "Case keys are decoded from pointer escapes, giving the a/b, c~d label of SLASH."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/web-flow-graph/spec.md#scenario-layers-order-coordinates-and-labels-of-a-small-flow", "quote": "`layoutFlow(S)` runs on `S` (reference.md), on `S` rebuilt with its node keys in reverse order and on a deep-frozen copy of `S`", "claim": "The scenario names only calls of layoutFlow and reads of two constants, with no page behaviour to observe."}]}
